# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HOST SCOPING (added 2026-09-11)
#
# The laptop (darwin) is the only machine that gets the full dotfiles: shell,
# ssh, editor, per-tool config. The Linux boxes are purpose-built servers whose
# shell config is genuinely different — ai-proxy's .zshrc is 90 lines against
# the laptop's 353, and its .zshenv/.bashrc were just corrected to remove
# account-pooling proxy exports. Pushing the laptop's copies there would undo
# that and break machine-specific setup.
#
# What servers DO get is the agent instruction layer, which is the thing that
# actually needs to be identical everywhere: ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md and
# ~/.claude/rules/. Their own agents/, commands/ and plugins/ stay local —
# ai-proxy has 24 agents and 72 commands of its own.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
{{ if ne .chezmoi.os "darwin" }}
.zshrc
.zshrc.secrets
.ssh/**
.config/nvim/**
.config/yazi/**
.config/opencode/**
.config/superpowers/**
.pixi/**
.gemini/**
.codex/**
.claude/agents/**
.claude/commands/**
.claude/plugins/**
.claude/settings.json
.claude/settings.local.json
AGENTS.md
{{ end }}


# ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md is TOOL-OWNED (added 2026-09-11). CodeGraph and lean-ctx
# write marked blocks into it and re-inject on every run, so managing it means
# chezmoi and those tools overwrite each other forever. On ai-proxy an apply
# deleted a lean-ctx block naming the alternatives to Grep/Glob -- which that
# host's settings.json actually denies. Shared content ships as
# .claude/rules/00-global.md instead; Claude Code loads all of ~/.claude/rules/.
.claude/CLAUDE.md

# ~/.zshrc.secrets is NOT managed (removed 2026-09-11). It is Mac-only, and the
# age-encrypted source entry made `chezmoi status` return EMPTY on every server
# that has no age key -- the error truncated the walk, so drift was invisible
# while `chezmoi apply` still overwrote files. Proven: appending a line to
# ~/.claude/rules/context7.md produced no status output and the next apply
# silently reverted it. Back this file up out-of-band; do not re-add it here.
.zshrc.secrets
